From f86f8f2ba9610e343376e0cb6a9b0c68f7c6c53a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SacredTrees <121399723+SacredTrees@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 02:21:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] WebCore: paths, strokes and gradients through OpenGPU

GraphicsContextOpenGPU draws fillPath, strokePath, strokeRect,
fillRoundedRect, fillRectWithRoundedHole and gradient fills itself, as
opengpu.library's PATH_FILL and PATH_STROKE (stream v1.6), where cairo
used to take them. Rectangles of one colour whose edges fall between
pixels, or that are turned, are anti-aliased paths too.

OpenGPU draws, as cairo would:
- paths of lines, quadratic and cubic curves, read from WebCore's own
  Path elements (applyElements), filled non-zero or even-odd, anti-aliased
  by each pixel's area inside them;
- strokes with cairo's own state, read from its context as cairo_stroke
  reads it: the width, butt, round and square caps, miter, round and bevel
  joins, the miter limit, and dashes from an offset (an odd count used
  twice; a dash of no length a dot or a square, as cairo's; a subpath of
  one point the same);
- a colour times the global alpha, or a linear or radial gradient (an
  elliptical one through its matrix, as GradientCairo.cpp makes it) with
  pad, repeat or reflect, the global alpha in its stops;
- by source-over, source-atop, destination-over, destination-out, xor and
  plus-lighter, which leave the pixels outside the path as they are.
cairo keeps copy and clear on paths (cairo bounds them by the path's
coverage, PATH_FILL by the clip), conic gradients (cairo's are a mesh),
gradients whose stops differ in alpha (pixman mixes them unpremultiplied,
OpenGPU premultiplied), patterns, shadows, other blend modes, paths with
anti-aliasing off, clips to paths, drawLine, drawRect and drawEllipse.

OpenGPUPaintAmiga.c writes each path into the batch's scratch words as it
comes, moving it to the start of scratch after sending the batch before
it when it needs the room; a path larger than all of scratch goes to
cairo. Scratch grows from 6 KB to 16 KB. The work memory PATH_FILL needs
is made when a path or picture first wants it.

Tested on the host against openamigartg's CPU core
(openamigabrowser tests/test_opengpu_paint.c): fills, strokes, joins,
caps, miter limits, dashes and gradients against a reference sampled 256
times a pixel.

